Description: enable VSync
 The intro never set the swap interval, so frames were swapped as fast as
 the driver allowed, depending on its default setting. Request VSync with
 SDL_GL_SetSwapInterval(1), right after the GL context is created.
Author: Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>
Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-17
--- a/src/intro.cpp
+++ b/src/intro.cpp
@@ -767,6 +767,12 @@
             exit(1);
         }
     }
+    // Synchronize buffer swaps with the display refresh rate. The context
+    // must be current, so this comes after SDL_GL_CreateContext().
+    if(SDL_GL_SetSwapInterval(1) != 0)
+    {
+        std::cerr << "WARNING: unable to enable VSync: " << SDL_GetError() << std::endl;
+    }
     if(!flag_fullscreen)
     {
         update_window_position();
